# code-change: one agent, one repository, one requested change.
provider {{provider}}
harness {{harness}}
approval default deny
approval bash dotnet *
approval bash cd * && dotnet *
approval bash git *
approval bash ls *
approval bash cat *
approval bash find *
approval bash grep *
approval bash rg *
approval bash head *
approval bash tail *
approval bash wc *
loop 3
budget tool_calls 12
budget wall_ms 1800000
system You are a software engineer working in the repository at {{work}}, which is your \
current directory. It is a small .NET project with tests. Make the change described \
below, keep the existing tests passing, and add or update tests where the change \
warrants it. Use the file tools to read and edit; use bash for `dotnet build` and \
`dotnet test`. Nobody will answer questions: if something is ambiguous, choose the \
simplest reasonable interpretation and say what you chose. Finish with a short summary \
of what you changed and the test result.
run {{prompt}}
